{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Take up the count of the captured spoil.</b> 'The captured spoil' (מלקוח) is the animal, and 'the captives' (השבי) are the people; its sense is 'the captured spoil and the captives,' in the manner of (Habakkuk 3:11) ״שמש ירח״ — 'sun [and] moon.' <b>And the heads of the fathers' houses of the congregation</b> — these are the princes (הנשיאים)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:22.631371849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}